@startuml
title ScheduNova - State Machine: User Account and Session (detailed)
hide empty description
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F7F9FB
  BorderColor #1D5B97
}

[*] --> Guest
state Guest : session user = "Guest"
Guest : do / can only call allow_guest methods (sign_up, login)

Guest --> SigningUp : submit sign-up form\nPOST schedunova.api.sign_up

state "Signing up (schedunova.api.sign_up)" as SigningUp {
  state RateCheck : do / frappe.rate_limiter.apply(limit=5, seconds=3600)
  state InputCheck : do / strip and lowercase email, strip name
  InputCheck : do / validate_email_address(email)
  state DuplicateCheck : do / frappe.db.exists("User", email)
  state Creating : do / insert User (Website User, enabled = 1)
  Creating : do / update_password(user, password)

  [*] --> RateCheck
  RateCheck --> InputCheck : [<= 5 attempts this hour]
  InputCheck --> DuplicateCheck : [all fields present and email valid]
  DuplicateCheck --> Creating : [email not registered]
}

RateCheck --> Guest : [> 5 attempts] / 429 Too Many Requests
InputCheck --> Guest : [field missing or bad email] / error
DuplicateCheck --> Guest : [email exists] / "Try logging in"
Creating --> Guest : [weak password] / throw, transaction rolled back
Creating --> Registered : [password accepted] / return {ok, user}

state Registered : enabled = 1, password hash in __Auth
Registered : no active session

Registered --> Authenticated : login(usr, pwd) [credentials ok]\n/ create session, Set-Cookie sid
Registered --> Registered : login [wrong password] / "Invalid login"

state Authenticated {
  state NoToken : session exists, no CSRF token yet
  state Ready : do / send X-Frappe-CSRF-Token on every write
  [*] --> NoToken
  NoToken --> Ready : get_csrf_token() / store token in UI
  Ready --> Ready : me() / return email, full_name
  Ready --> Ready : create, edit, delete own Nova Tasks
}

Authenticated --> Registered : logout / delete session
Authenticated --> Registered : session expires
Registered --> Disabled : System Manager sets enabled = 0
Authenticated --> Disabled : System Manager sets enabled = 0\n/ sessions cleared
state Disabled : enabled = 0, login refused
Disabled --> Registered : System Manager sets enabled = 1
Disabled --> [*] : user deleted

note right of Authenticated
  me() throws AuthenticationError (401)
  whenever session user is "Guest".
end note
@enduml
